WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Pushkar> Hi Sneha, thanks so much for joining me today. I'm a Product Manager at Myntra.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.000
<v Sneha> Hi Pushkar! No problem at all, I shop on Myntra practically every week, so happy to chat.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Pushkar> That's great to hear. I'd love to start by asking about your general experience with the app recently. What's working well for you?

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Sneha> I will say, your return pickup process is the absolute best in the industry. The delivery guy comes the exact next day, no questions asked. 

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Sneha> It makes me feel safe buying from Myntra compared to Ajio or Nykaa.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Pushkar> I'm really glad to hear the logistics side is smooth! Is there anything that frustrates you during the shopping experience?

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:44.000
<v Sneha> Actually, yes. It is incredibly frustrating when I filter by 'Delivery by Tomorrow' for a last-minute party outfit. 

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Sneha> The app shows me a dress, I spend 20 minutes deciding, but when I finally reach the checkout page, it suddenly says delivery will take 3 days.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.000
<v Sneha> It feels like a bait-and-switch. If I filter for tomorrow, the checkout needs to honor that.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Pushkar> Oh, that is definitely a broken experience. The delivery estimate should update on the product page, not at checkout. 

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Pushkar> Have you noticed any other issues, maybe around sizing or finding clothes?

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:13.000
<v Sneha> Yes, sizing is a huge gamble. I am on the curvier side, and every single dress is modeled on someone who is 5'9 and super skinny.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:21.000
<v Sneha> I really wish there was a feature to see clothes on models with similar body types to mine. Like a virtual try-on, or just showing diverse models.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Sneha> I end up returning 40% of what I buy simply because the fit looks completely different on my body.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:32.000
<v Pushkar> That makes total sense. An inclusive sizing visualizer is something we've been discussing. One last question: how do you feel about the refund process?

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Sneha> Well, I was very confused last week. I returned a kurta, and the app automatically refunded it to 'Myntra Credit' instead of my bank account.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:49.000
<v Sneha> There was no clear warning that the default refund method had changed. I had to email support to get it transferred back to my UPI. 

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Pushkar> I apologize for that, we recently updated the default to speed up refunds, but the communication clearly wasn't there. 

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Pushkar> Thank you so much for your time, Sneha. This is exactly the kind of feedback our team needs.
